commit 885b5e0294e3d67ae20bf46e8d32d732c5d70a13
Author: Liz <liz@gewelf.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 22:23:57 2026 -0400

    hardening: free partial allocations on OOM in nested assembly and footer parse

    assembleRecursive leaked the assembled list item when append failed, and
    the assembled struct field value plus its name copy when the name dupe or
    append failed. Add errdefers for each.

    FileMetaData.parse had no cleanup, so a mid-parse error leaked the schema,
    row groups, key-value metadata and created_by. Add FileMetaData.deinit
    (frees the tree parse builds, skipping defaulted fields) and per-element
    errdefers for the three lists. Sibling parsers (ColumnChunk, Statistics,
    RowGroup, SchemaElement, KeyValue) still leak internally on OOM; that
    needs errdefers in format/*.zig and is not covered here.

    Adds a FailingAllocator sweep test for assembleValues. Verified it fails
    without the errdefers.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M67WAPQ8ZC3VK276X45X5VMC

 zig-parquet/src/core/format/metadata.zig | 91 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 zig-parquet/src/core/nested.zig          | 49 +++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 131 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)
